--- A function value compared with text (`f eq 'a'`) passes the checks.
--- Interpreted (crow run -i): prints `false`, exit 0.
--- Compiled (crow run): does not build —
---   error[E0308]: mismatched types
---   error: the compiled program does not build — the Rust compiler refused what Crow
---   accepted, a bug in Crow, not in this program (`crow run -i` runs it meanwhile)
--- Expected: refused before the program runs in both modes, as `x eq 'a'` of a number is
--- ("eq compares values of one kind, not a number with text"). The same happens to a
--- parameter handed a function and compared with text inside the function
--- (`fn pick[f]` / `if f eq 'loop'`, called `pick[one]`), which is how it was met.

fn one[]
    return 1

f = one
log[f eq 'a']
